From: Andrew Hunt <achunt@bellsouth.net>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Report the foreground card to WebOSCompositorBase

getForegroundAppInfo always returned an empty list, on both
com.webos.surfacemanager and com.webos.service.applicationmanager, no matter
what was on screen. Anything keying off the foreground app was therefore
broken - most visibly, taps fell through a focused app to the launcher
underneath, so tapping over an open app could bring up Just Type. QML apps
were unaffected because they take a different path.

Cause: WebOSCompositorBase/Views.qml declares

    foregroundItems: Utils.foregroundList(viewsRoot.children)

and ForegroundAppInfoMgr feeds that to getForegroundAppInfo.
Utils.foregroundList() walks viewsRoot's DIRECT children looking for one with
hasForegroundItem == true and a currentItem whose displayId >= 0.

LuneOS overrides the ViewsRoot type in its qmldir with LuneOSViewRoot.qml, and
keeps its windows in its own tree (CardShell -> CardsArea -> CardView) instead
of the base views. So viewsRoot's only child was OrientationHelper, nothing
ever had hasForegroundItem, and the list stayed empty forever.

Add a small proxy child of the view root that supplies exactly what
foregroundList() looks for, and expose the CardView up through CardsArea and
CardShell so it can be reached.

currentItem is assigned imperatively rather than bound because
currentActiveWindow() is a function call and creates no binding dependency;
assigning it emits currentItemChanged, which re-runs the outer foregroundItems
binding. The timer is a safety net: currentCardChanged() is only emitted when
the card GROUP index changes, while selecting a different card within a group
goes through listCardGroupsModel.setCurrentCard() and emits nothing, and
currentActiveWindow() ultimately depends on a ListModel role that cannot be
bound to. refresh() only assigns on a real change, so it emits nothing while
the foreground is stable.

Verified on bluejay: both services now report the on-screen app, and the
reported app tracks card switches.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/qml/LuneOSViewRoot.qml
+++ b/qml/LuneOSViewRoot.qml
@@ -44,4 +44,75 @@
             z: 1 // above the main shell
         }
     }
+
+    // --- foreground reporting bridge ---------------------------------
+    // WebOSCompositorBase/Views.qml declares
+    //     foregroundItems: Utils.foregroundList(viewsRoot.children)
+    // and ForegroundAppInfoMgr feeds that to getForegroundAppInfo.
+    // foregroundList() walks viewsRoot's CHILDREN looking for one with
+    // hasForegroundItem == true and a currentItem whose displayId >= 0.
+    //
+    // LuneOS overrides the ViewsRoot type (see qmldir) with this file, and
+    // keeps its windows in its own tree (CardShell -> CardsArea -> CardView)
+    // rather than in the base views. So no child ever had hasForegroundItem
+    // and getForegroundAppInfo returned an empty list forever - which is why
+    // taps fell through to the launcher instead of the focused app.
+    //
+    // This proxy child supplies exactly what foregroundList() looks for.
+    // currentItem is assigned imperatively rather than bound, because
+    // currentActiveWindow() is a function call and would create no binding
+    // dependency; the assignment emits currentItemChanged, which re-runs the
+    // outer foregroundItems binding.
+    Item {
+        id: foregroundProxy
+        visible: false
+        width: 0
+        height: 0
+
+        property bool hasForegroundItem: true
+        property bool grouped: false
+        property var groupedItems: null
+        property bool hasMultiItems: false
+        property var items: []
+        property var currentItem: null
+
+        function refresh() {
+            var shell = mainShellLoader.item;
+            var area = shell && shell.cardsAreaInstance ? shell.cardsAreaInstance : null;
+            var view = area && area.cardView ? area.cardView : null;
+            var next = view ? view.currentActiveWindow() : null;
+            if (currentItem !== next)
+                currentItem = next;
+        }
+    }
+
+    Connections {
+        target: mainShellLoader.item && mainShellLoader.item.cardsAreaInstance
+                ? mainShellLoader.item.cardsAreaInstance.cardView : null
+        ignoreUnknownSignals: true
+        function onCurrentCardChanged() { foregroundProxy.refresh(); }
+    }
+
+    // Safety net. currentCardChanged() is only emitted when the card GROUP
+    // index changes (CardGroupListView.internalListView.onCurrentIndexChanged);
+    // selecting a different card WITHIN a group goes through
+    // listCardGroupsModel.setCurrentCard() and emits nothing, so re-raising an
+    // already-running app left the reported foreground app stale.
+    // currentActiveWindow() also depends on a ListModel role, which cannot be
+    // bound to. Two property reads on a slow timer is cheap and keeps the
+    // reported state correct regardless of which path changed the current card;
+    // refresh() only assigns on a real change, so no spurious notifications.
+    Timer {
+        id: foregroundPoll
+        interval: 400
+        repeat: true
+        running: true
+        onTriggered: foregroundProxy.refresh()
+    }
+
+    Connections {
+        target: mainShellLoader
+        ignoreUnknownSignals: true
+        function onLoaded() { foregroundProxy.refresh(); }
+    }
 }
--- a/qml/CardShell.qml
+++ b/qml/CardShell.qml
@@ -37,6 +37,9 @@
 Rectangle {
     id: root
 
+
+    // Exposed so the view root can reach the card view (foreground reporting).
+    property alias cardsAreaInstance: cardsArea
     color: "black"
     state: cardShellState // inherited from the main shell Loader
 
--- a/qml/CardsArea.qml
+++ b/qml/CardsArea.qml
@@ -42,6 +42,10 @@
 WindowManager {
     id: windowManager
 
+    // Exposed so the view root can report the foreground card to
+    // WebOSCompositorBase (see LuneOSViewRoot.qml).
+    property alias cardView: cardViewInstance
+
     property real screenwidth: windowManager.width
     property real screenheight: windowManager.height
     property real screenDPI: Settings.dpi
